From 90a2796921d98ecfb8c3a69097d950de74dc46f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W1nkelm4nn <mrmarkap61@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:18:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kk: Add MESA_KK_NULL_IMAGE_SELECT

Every image and texture access through a descriptor that may be null is
wrapped in a branch. Shaders reading thousands of textures, as some of
Horizon Zero Dawn's compute shaders do, become large and slow to compile:
the largest took 14.4 s in Metal's front end, 8.6 s with reads selecting
zero for null descriptors instead, and 2.3 s without any null handling.
Apple GPUs read through a null resource ID without faulting on the M3
(Horizon Zero Dawn, Green Hell, Kebab Chefs, Medieval Dynasty). But the
branch skips the reads, and vkd3d-proton binds many null descriptors:
Medieval Dynasty ran at 15-20 instead of 22 fps with selects, Green Hell
and Kebab Chefs a little faster. So it stays an option, and it is part of
the pipeline cache key, as are the disabled workarounds.

Generated-by: LLM
